OVERVIEW: Run a short-lived process without creating a project.

The command starts in the background, returns a job ID immediately, and is
stopped with its entire process group at the timeout. Use 'portly wait <id>' to
collect the result.

USAGE: portly temp [<command>] [--name <name>] [--command <command>] [--path <path>] [--port <port>] [--health-url <health-url>] [--timeout <timeout>] [--env <env> ...] [--json] [--api-port <api-port>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <command>               Command to run through a login shell, for example
                          'npm run build'.

OPTIONS:
  --name <name>           Short label shown in Portly. Defaults to the command.
  --command <command>     Command option kept for compatibility; prefer the
                          positional command.
  --path <path>           Working directory. Defaults to the current directory.
                          (default:
                          /private/var/folders/7z/5mtgxwxx4zs9ppgzm942gbmh0000gn/T/workspace.TlYDeu/app)
  --port <port>           Optional port to monitor.
  --health-url <health-url>
                          Optional health check path or URL.
  --timeout <timeout>     Maximum runtime: seconds or a value such as 30s, 10m,
                          or 2h. (default: 30m)
  --env <env>             Environment variables as KEY=VALUE.
  --json                  Print raw JSON instead of a human summary.
  --api-port <api-port>   Override the control API port.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

===
Error: Portly is not running and could not be launched. Open Portly.app, then retry.
